                "KLiNQ illustrates a different evidence chain. It classifies measured signals from superconducting qubits using a compact model designed for an FPGA, whose logic can be configured after manufacture. Its evaluation includes classification accuracy, implementation resources, and processing delay. These quantities answer different questions. Accurate classification does not establish that the computation fits or finishes in time; a fast implementation does not establish accurate classification. Measured input signals also do not, by themselves, make every reported processing or system-level quantity a physical measurement.",
